Classic cards XMage lacked, batch 2, as printed (Commander Duels v0.9.5): Frankenstein's Monster and
Reflecting Mirror (The Dark), Suffocation (Alliances), Equinox, Silhouette, Backdraft, Quarum Trench
Gnomes and North Star (Legends), Arcum's Whistle, Winter's Chill and Spoils of War (Ice Age), and
Ogre Enforcer (Visions).

Reason: Commander Duels deals these cards from their sets' packs, and XMage had no implementation
of them, so they played as stand-ins. No new core piece: each card carries its own effects and
watchers. Where the printed wording leaves a choice to the engine:
- Spoils of War's X is set as it is cast, from the opponent whose graveyard holds the most artifact
  and creature cards (with one opponent, theirs).
- North Star's "one spell" is the next spell its controller casts that turn.
- Silhouette's "sources that target it" are spells and abilities on the stack targeting the
  creature as they deal the damage.
- Ogre Enforcer counts the damage marked on it per source for the turn.
- Equinox's "would destroy a land you control": a mode that destroys a target land you control, or
  that destroys all permanents of a kind its words name as lands.
- Reflecting Mirror's spell is chosen as the ability is activated, so X is set to twice its mana
  value.
Upstream: none.
Remove when: XMage implements these cards.
